# SRG-APP-000925-AU-000420  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must compare the internal system clocks on an
# organization-defined frequency with organization-defined authoritative
# time source.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000925-AU-000420
group:           V-263585
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004923
control_rev5:    SC-45

contribution:    Splunk compares its own clock against each search peer's clock when the
                 peer is registered and on distributed searches, and expresses the
                 tolerated difference through addpeer_skew_limit and max_tolerable_skew;
                 the comparison frequency and the authoritative source are not application
                 settings.

governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.

check:           limits.conf [search] addpeer_skew_limit present
check:           limits.conf [search] max_tolerable_skew present

external:        The host operating system's time service, which performs the comparison
                 against the authoritative time source and corrects the clock
external:        The organization-defined comparison frequency and the identity of the
                 authoritative time source, which are policy determinations the application
                 cannot hold
external:        Operating system STIG settings for the time service, such as the chrony or
                 ntpd polling interval

citation:        SRG-APP-000925-AU-000420 check text; limits.conf.spec:180, 493-502,
                 529-536, 3676
finding:         Splunk expresses no tolerated difference for the clock comparison it
                 performs against its search peers (limits.conf [search] max_tolerable_skew
                 or addpeer_skew_limit is not available in the assessed configuration), so
                 a divergent peer clock is neither reported nor refused.
